[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3126646824","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109018#issuecomment-3126646824","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109018","id":3126646824,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc66XNgo","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-07-28T10:47:05Z","updated_at":"2025-07-28T10:47:05Z","body":"That would indeed seem to be a bug of some sort.\n\nI'll have to do a deeper dive at some later point to see if this is on our end or an upstream Jolt issue.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3126646824/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3315229668","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109018#issuecomment-3315229668","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109018","id":3315229668,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FmmPk","user":{"login":"jrouwe","id":1621693,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjE2OTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1621693?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe","html_url":"https://github.com/jrouwe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-20T20:11:18Z","updated_at":"2025-09-20T20:11:18Z","body":"This is an issue in Jolt. Locking an axis causes zeros in the inverse inertia matrix. This makes the matrix singular and causes the constraint to turn itself off (to prevent NaNs from entering the system). I don't know yet how I'm going to fix this...","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3315229668/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3315687832","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109018#issuecomment-3315687832","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109018","id":3315687832,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FoWGY","user":{"login":"jrouwe","id":1621693,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjE2OTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1621693?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe","html_url":"https://github.com/jrouwe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-21T08:08:36Z","updated_at":"2025-09-21T08:08:36Z","body":"B.t.w. there is a very simple workaround for this issue: Don't try to constrain rotation around an axis that is locked. In the case of this 6DOF joint: If you make X and Y free and only constrain Z then the problem is gone. \n\n<img width=\"281\" height=\"1170\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/19ba1daa-eb34-4d6c-a17e-a7d4cd5e79da\" />\n\nIntuitively, you can see that locking a rotation axis gives infinite resistance to rotation around that axis. A constraint that works around that axis needs to be able to provide enough torque to make the body rotate. This means it needs to provide infinite torque to counter the infinite resistance to rotation. This is not possible, so doesn't work.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3315687832/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3315925921","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109018#issuecomment-3315925921","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109018","id":3315925921,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FpQOh","user":{"login":"mihe","id":4884246,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ4ODQyNDY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4884246?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe","html_url":"https://github.com/mihe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mihe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-21T11:12:10Z","updated_at":"2025-09-21T11:12:10Z","body":"> Don't try to constrain rotation around an axis that is locked. In the case of this 6DOF joint: If you make X and Y free and only constrain Z then the problem is gone.\n\nI assume this only works so long as the constraint/joint happens to be aligned with the world axes when created?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3315925921/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3315929330","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/109018#issuecomment-3315929330","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/109018","id":3315929330,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7FpRDy","user":{"login":"jrouwe","id":1621693,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjE2OTM=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1621693?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe","html_url":"https://github.com/jrouwe","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jrouwe/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-09-21T11:18:49Z","updated_at":"2025-09-21T11:18:49Z","body":"As long as the constraint is aligned with some world axis, you would need to make the axis free that point in the world X and Y direction (for this particular example). If the constraint is not aligned with any world axis then yes this wouldn't work.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3315929330/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]